id: pm-8pnj
title: "Golden agent-transcript replay: measure tokens-per-completed-task as a CI-visible DX regression gate"
description: "Replay versioned golden agent task transcripts in CI to measure and gate total tokens per completed task, complementing context-quality evaluation."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:ci",measurement,simplification
created_at: "2026-07-11T16:22:48.239Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T11:53:56.933Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T11:53:56.333Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T11:53:56.333Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Golden transcript corpus (canonical agent task sequences) versioned in-repo; replay runner reports bytes+approx-tokens per completed task against the current build; wired into the existing token-cost CI gate lineage with a documented regression threshold; boundary with pm-atfm quality harness documented; workflow for adding transcripts documented
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Published a versioned multi-step agent-task transcript SDK contract with executable refusal recovery, per-step accounting-mode invariants, and a ratcheted real-transport token baseline."
expected_result: "Release gates replay complete representative workflows, fail on output, recovery, token, identity, or accounting-mode drift, and retain exact registry-independent transport evidence."
actual_result: Transcript v2 and baseline v3 now bind all 14 real steps to observed self-reported or independent accounting modes; the 5-task budget remains 4349 estimated tokens.
